   "": {
    "actClause": "AN ACT to amend the state finance law, the highway law and the public\nauthorities law, in relation to certain contracts involving industrial\npainting and industrial coatings",
    "basePrintNo": "S5517",
    "basePrintNoStr": "S5517-2021",
    "coSponsors": {
     "items": [],
     "size": 0
    },
    "fullText": "",
    "fullTextFormats": [],
    "fullTextHtml": "",
    "fullTextTemplate": "",
    "lawCode": "Add §136-d, St Fin L; amd §38, Hway L; amd §1285-s, Pub Auth L",
    "lawSection": "State Finance Law",
    "memo": "\n \nBILL NUMBER: S5517\n\nSPONSOR: KENNEDY\n \nTITLE OF BILL:\n\nAn act to amend the state finance law, the highway law and the public\nauthorities law, in relation to certain contracts involving industrial\npainting and industrial coatings\n\n \nSUMMARY OF PROVISIONS:\n\nSection 1: Amends the state finance law to provide that any contract\nreceiving state financial assistance that includes industrial painting\nor coating shall include workers certified to conduct the work.\n\nSection 2: Amends the highway law to provide that any highway contracts\nmust follow the provisions set in section one.\n\nSection 3: Provides that any intermunicipal water quality infrastructure\nprojects must follow the same training requirements for industrial\npainting and coating projects.\n\nSection 4: Sets the effective date.\n\n \nJUSTIFICATION:\n\nWhen approving state money for industrial painting and coating projects,\nit is important that workers are qualified to perform the work in a safe\nand efficient manner. The SSPC Coating Application Specialist Certif-\nication Program is an industry approved training course that trains both\nunion and non-union painting and coating workers. These workers are\ntrained.on how to perform work safely to avoid serious injury, how to\nbest apply coats so that the work performed lasts for the life of the\nproject, and how to properly dispose of dangerous chemicals used in the\npainting process. Further, the industrial painting industry has become\nmore complex, leading to different levels of skill depending on the\ncompany selected.\n\nOther states, including Connecticut, have enacted standards in state\nfunded contracts that incorporate SSPC training in painting and coating\ncontracts. By incorporating similar standards in New York, painting and\ncoating jobs will be performed correctly from the start, avoiding the\nneed to go back and redo any jobs that were not performed correctly.\n\n \nFISCAL IMPACT:\n\nNone.\n\n \nPRIOR LEGISLATIVE HISTORY:\n\n2017-18: S.843/A.11349\n\n2019-20: S.3561A/A.2337A\n\n \nEFFECTIVE DATE:\nThis act shall take effect immediately.\n",
