    "lawCode": "Add §136-d, St Fin L",
    "lawSection": "State Finance Law",
    "memo": "\n \nBILL NUMBER: S5517A\n\nSPONSOR: KENNEDY\n \nTITLE OF BILL:\n\nAn act to amend the state finance law, in relation to certain contracts\ninvolving industrial painting and industrial coatings\n\n \nPURPOSE OR GENERAL IDEA OF BILL:\n\nThis bill would establish procurement guidelines for the procurement and\napplication of industrial paints and industrial coatings.\n\n \nSUMMARY OF PROVISIONS:\n\nSection 1 of the bill requires the Office of General Services to estab-\nlish guidelines concerning the procurement of industrial painting and\nindustrial coating. Contractors doing this type of work would then need\nto follow these guidelines and certify that their work meets these mini-\nmum standards. The bill outlines what the office will need to examine\nwhen crafting the guidelines.\n\nSection 2 of the bill is the effective date.\n\n \nJUSTIFICATION:\n\nWhen approving state money for industrial painting and coating projects,\nit is important that workers are qualified to perform the work in a safe\nand efficient manner. It is important that these workers are trained on\nhow to perform work safely to avoid serious injury, how to best apply\ncoats so that the work performed lasts for the life of the project, and\nhow to properly dispose of dangerous chemicals used in the painting\nprocess. Further, the industrial painting industry has become more\ncomplex, leading to different levels of skill depending on the company\nselected. Other states, including Connecticut, have enacted standards in\nstate funded contracts that incorporate specific trainings in painting\nand coating contracts. By incorporating similar standards in New York,\npainting and coating jobs will be performed correctly from the start,\navoiding the need to go back and redo any jobs that were not performed\ncorrectly.\n\n \nPRIOR LEGISLATIVE HISTORY:\n\n2019-2020: S.3561 Passed Senate/A.2337 - Referred to Governmental Oper-\nations\n\n2017-2018: S.8843 Referred to Finance/A.11349 - Referred to Governmental\nOperations.\n\n \nFISCAL IMPLICATIONS FOR STATE AND LOCAL GOVERNMENTS:\n\nNone\n\n \nEFFECTIVE DATE:\nThis act shall take effect on the one hundred eightieth day and shall\napply to any state contracting opportunities advertised on or after such\ndate and shall exclude contracts for which an invitation for bid,\nrequest for proposal, or similar solicitation has been issued prior to\nthe effective date of this act.\n",
